computing/INSTALL

(2020-Nov-11: Not up to date.  --JH)

This tells you how to run LaTeX on the source of the book.  See also the
README.

1) The book's graphics are made with Asymptote. So you must install
that.  Then you must get Asymptote to search the desired directory
by putting something like this in /etc/profile (obviously your home
directory may differ).

  # Asymptote drawing program
  export ASYMPTOTE_DIR=$HOME/Documents/computing/src/asy/asy-graphtheory-master/modules

2) There is some programming in Scheme.  So to run those you need that.

3) There is a builder script, but it needs revision.

  cd src
  ./00build.sh


========================================
2021 Notes

0) Fresh Ubuntu 20 install, from scratch.  Fresh TeX Live, from the web install.

1) To get Asymptote to run:
  a) need to install libglut.
  b) need to install imagemagick
  c) In /etc/ImageMagick-6/policy.xml needed to change lines about PS, PDF, etc
  from rights="none" to rights="read|write".
  d) Put these lines at the end of your profile file in your home directory,
  where you need to change /Documents/computing to wherever you put the repo.

# Directories for the Asymptote drawing program
export ASYMPTOTE_DIR=$HOME/Documents/computing/src/asy:$HOME/Documents/computing/src/asy/asy-graphtheory-master/modules:$ASYMPTOTE_DIR

  Then log out and log in again (which is the simplest way to run the profile).
  Then open a terminal and run "echo $ASYMPTOTE_DIR" to see that the
  environment variable is set.


  